invariant: INV-68
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh x86-kernels
reason: rsa_sign64.c runs a signature's exponentiations on rsa_mont64_adx.c
  under the multiply bit alone, whatever CH_CPU_BMI2_ADX says, so a session
  on a CPU without BMI2 or ADX dies of SIGILL at its first signature. On a
  CPU with them every byte stays right, so no vector notices.
  bin/x86_kernels_test counts the calls into rsa_mont64_adx.c under each
  ch_cfg.cpu value, and the qemu lane runs it for x86-64, the one
  architecture whose signer holds the test.

--- old
    uint32_t both = CH_CPU_BMI2_ADX | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY;
--- new
    uint32_t both = CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY;
